    "html": "<p>The left end of a metal cube is held at a constant temperature <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>, while its right end is held at a constant temperature of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3T\"></span>. The side length of the cube is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span> and the rate of thermal energy transfer through the cube is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The left and right ends of a cube made of the same metal are held at temperatures <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2T\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5T\"></span>, respectively. Given that the side length of this cube is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2L\"></span>, what is the thermal energy transfer through this cube?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3R\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6R\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"12R\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"24R\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
